<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torgils Knutsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1306">1306</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Torgils Knutsson was Lord High Constable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and the leading figure of the regency for the young King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birger-jarl">Birger Magnusson</a> in the 1290s. In 1293 he led the expedition into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a> known as the third Swedish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vyborg">Vyborg</a> Castle. He fell from power after conflict with the king's brothers and the church, and was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> in 1306.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torgils-knutsson.jpg" alt="Torgils Knutsson" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrew Zorin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torkel_Knutsson_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
